            <div xml:id="d196">

                <pb facs="0168" n="162" sameAs="frus:frus1939v04/pg162"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.102 Kulangsu/268: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Amoy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >MacVitty</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Amoy</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-10-18T11:00:00+08:00">October 18, 1939—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received October 18—2 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to Embassy’s telegram October 17, 9 p.m. The American and Japanese
                    landing forces will simultaneously withdraw from <pb facs="0169" n="163"
                        xml:id="pg163"/> the International Settlement at 2 p.m., today. The request
                    for simultaneous withdrawal was made by the Japanese authorities.</p>
                <p>Sent to Peiping. Repeated to Chungking and Shanghai. Peiping repeat to Tokyo.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">MacVitty</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
